# WLISTTW.KEY - more of the list window's dividers (TEST/WLISTT.C), on
# the seed's three items: TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WLISTTW.SNP.  The keys are
# those of WLISTTV.KEY, with W a one-pixel move, Y the rows wl_rows fits
# in a window of the list's width and S the list made again without
# dividers, then with them.
S START
K Y
S ROWS0
# Cat, which keeps no width, dragged one pixel: less than half an
# average character, so nothing is stored and no note comes.
K SHIFT-J J I W Q
S ONEPX
K V
S STORE0
# ID widened past the window: the stored width alone brings the bar in,
# and wl_rows fits a row fewer.
K SHIFT-J I K Q
S WIDEN
K Y
S ROWS1
# Without WL_SIZES: a press on Cat's divider is on its flat heading, no
# guide shows, the release stores nothing.
K S
S PLAIN
K SHIFT-J J I K Z
S NOGUIDE
K Q V
S NOSTORE
# A press just inside ID's right edge, in the SERIAL order, is a click
# on ID's button: the list goes back to the ID order.
K TAB
S SERIAL
K SHIFT-J SHIFT-I Q
S CLICKID
# With WL_SIZES again, the same press is on the divider: nothing moves.
K S TAB
S SIZED
K SHIFT-J SHIFT-I Q
S NOCLICK
